# View Patterns

Reference implementation: `app.rnc/src/modules/User/views/Users/UsersView.view.vue` and its `RULES.md` — a server-paginated `OListDivided` with `OPaginator`, add/edit dialog and confirm popups.

These patterns apply to authenticated list/detail views in app.rnc. Auth flows (`Login`, `SignUp`, etc.) use `TheCenteredLayout` instead — do not force this structure there.

## Page structure

```vue
<TheLayout>
  <template #pageHeader>
    <ThePageHeader icon="pi pi-user" title="users.title">
      <template v-if="!dialogVisible" #actions>
        <!-- CTA buttons -->
      </template>
    </ThePageHeader>
  </template>

  <!-- filters, grids, main content -->

  <aside class="contents">
    <!-- ConfirmPopup + MMainDialog only -->
  </aside>
</TheLayout>
```

- **`TheLayout` + `#pageHeader` + `ThePageHeader`** — never put page headers in the default slot (see `TheLayout/RULES.md`).
- **`<aside class="contents">` at the end** — holds all overlays; keeps dialog mask scoping with `MMainDialog`'s `appendTo="self"`.
  The `contents` class is not optional. The overlays draw nothing in flow, but a box here is still a
  flex child of `TheLayout`'s content column, whose `gap-8` reserves 32px under the page for it — a
  dead band, and 32px taken from anything sized to fill the height. An organism with an `<aside>`
  beside its root has the same problem wherever it is placed.
- **Hide header actions while a dialog is open**: `v-if="!dialogVisible"` on `#actions`.

## MMainDialog (create/edit)

- **Always `MMainDialog`** — never raw PrimeVue `<Dialog>`.
- **`isFooterless`** for create/edit flows — the form molecule owns submit/cancel (sticky footer via `form="…-form"`).
- **`title` is an i18n key** — `MMainDialog` calls `$t()` internally; never pass a pre-translated string.
- **`:key` on the form molecule**: `:key="editingEntity?.id ?? 'new'"` — mandatory so PrimeVue Forms resets between create and edit.

See `MMainDialog/RULES.md` for mask scoping, animation, and scroll-lock contracts.

## Form molecule contract

Extract inline forms to `MAddEdit{Entity}Form` under the module's `components/molecules/`.

| Responsibility | Owner |
| --- | --- |
| Form fields, Yup validation, API call | Form molecule |
| Dialog visibility, list state | Parent view |
| Submit/cancel buttons (footerless dialog) | Form molecule |

- **Prop**: entity prop (`user`, `profile`, etc.) — `null`/`undefined` = create, object = edit.
- **Emits**: `@onClose` and `@onSuccess(entity)` where `entity` is the API response body.
- **Do not** refetch the full list from inside the molecule — parent updates local refs.

## Managed lists: paginated on the server

A list that can grow is a page, not the table. The API answers `ApiResponse::paginated` and the view
uses `usePaginatedList` (`@Composables`) + `<OPaginator>` — never hand-rolled page state, never
PrimeVue `<Paginator>` directly.

- **Sort, filter and search go back to page 1** (`page.value = 1; load()`).
- **Row-level actions that open a confirm popup go in `OListDivided`'s `#actions` slot**, not in
  `canArchive`/`canDelete`: the popup needs the clicked element as its anchor, and the built-in
  buttons emit only the item. Render per `variant` (`inline` icon, `menu` labeled).

## List mutations (granular)

Use the entity returned by the API — no full refetch when the response includes the saved record.

- **Create**: `prependItem(entity)` — it counts the row and returns to page 1 when needed.
- **Create while a filter or search is applied**: reload page 1 (`page.value = 1; load()`) instead
  of prepending. The new row was not in the search, and a row above the matches reads as a broken
  search. "Applied" is what the last request SENT, not what the person picked and has not searched
  yet (`UsersView`'s `appliedSearch`).
- **Update**: replace by ID in `items` (the count does not change).
- **Delete**: `removeItem(id)` — it decrements the total and steps back from a page it emptied.
- **Archive**: replace by ID using the API response.
- **Never write `items.value = [...]` to add or remove a row** on a paginated list: the pager keeps
  offering a page that no longer exists.

## Permissions

Define `canCreate`, `canRead`, `canUpdate`, `canDelete`, etc. as computed properties from `userStore.hasPermission('resource.action')` in the view — not inside card/list child components.

**A missing permission hides the part that needs it; it never becomes a grant.** When a step, a tab
or a panel depends on a key the person does not hold, leave it out — do not mount the component —
and never add the permission to a role "so the screen stops looking broken". The screen that
vanished is the permission working.

## Destructive actions

- **`useConfirm()` + `<ConfirmPopup>`** with distinct `group` values per action type.
- **Never `<ConfirmDialog>`** for row-level archive/delete.
- Views may inline `confirm.require({ ... })` with custom `acceptProps`/`rejectProps` (see `UsersView.view.vue`) instead of `MConfirmPopup` when action-specific styling is needed.
- **A destructive action that needs input is a form, not a popup.** When cancelling asks for a
  reason, or a choice (refund or not), it is a form molecule in `MMainDialog`, under the same contract as `MAddEdit{Entity}Form` —
  a `ConfirmPopup` holds no fields, and a popup with inputs squeezed in is a screen no test can
  drive. The popup stays for the plain yes/no (largatudoevai's `MCancelReservationForm`).

## A load that failed is not an empty list

"Nobody has written anything yet" and "we could not reach the server" ask opposite things of the
reader, so they are different screens: the empty state says what to do next, the failure says the
list did not load and offers **Try again**. Rendering the empty state after a failed request tells
the person their data is gone. A `404` for the thing being opened is "does not exist"; any other
failure — network, 5xx — is "did not load".

And a refresh that follows a save is **returned**, not fired and forgotten: a toast that says "saved"
while the list beside it silently fails to refresh is a screen that lies.

## Polling

- **One poller per screen, and the view owns it.** The view starts it, stops it on unmount and passes
  what it learns down. A molecule that polls is a molecule that polls twice when a screen shows two
  of it, and keeps polling after the view that needed it is gone.
- **A poller has two ceilings: time and consecutive failures.** It stops after a fixed total duration
  (a payment that has not settled in ten minutes will not settle by being asked every three seconds)
  and after N failures in a row (an API that is down is not helped by a request every few seconds
  from every open tab). Reaching either says so on screen, with a way to check again — never a
  spinner that turns forever. A success resets the failure count; only a run of them stops it.
- **It pauses when the screen is hidden and resumes when it is seen again.** On
  `visibilitychange` to hidden, stop; back to visible — or when the person reopens the screen —
  check once right away and start again with fresh ceilings. A background tab is not someone waiting.

## Refusals from the API (422)

A 422 is the API refusing on a rule, and it names the rule with an i18n key (`errors.<field>[0]`).
It is information, not a failure:

- **In a form**: show the translated key inline, where the problem is, and raise no toast — a generic
  "something went wrong" on top contradicts the specific message.
- **From a row action**: a `warn` toast with `translateError(key)` and no "refresh and contact the
  admin" detail. Only what is NOT a 422 is the red error toast.

## Do not

- Put `MMainDialog` or `ConfirmPopup` outside `<aside>` — in a VIEW. The exception is a molecule used
  on a full page rather than in a list (a wizard step, a picker that creates inline): it may own its
  `MMainDialog`, the way `OListDivided` owns its detail dialog. The `<aside>` rule exists for mask
  scoping over a list, and a full-page flow has no list for the mask to scope. Say so in the
  molecule's `RULES.md`.
- Inline a form inside `MMainDialog` — extract to `MAddEdit{Entity}Form`.
- Refetch the entire list after a single create/update/delete when the API returns the entity.
